"""
Measured values of an application -- requests, logins, errors, the size of
a queue -- kept in its SQLite database and read back as a series of
buckets for a chart (Wolly.Svg).

A sample is a name, a time in seconds since 1970 and a value of 0 or more.
A series is the samples of one name from a start, cut into buckets of
step seconds each, at most mostBuckets of them; a bucket is the sum or the
largest of its samples, 0 when it has none.  Old samples are pruned by the
caller (pruneMetrics), as the audit log is.

SQLite and not a column store: the number of samples of one application
is small for SQLite (an index over name and time answers a series).
"""
import Standard.Buffer (
    Buffer
);
import Standard.Database (
    Database,
    Writing,
    DbError
);

module Wolly.Metrics is
    """
    How a bucket is made of its samples.
    """
    union Fold: Free is
        """
        The sum: counts, such as requests.
        """
        case Total;
        """
        The largest: levels, such as the length of a queue.
        """
        case Highest;
    end;

    """
    The most buckets of a series: 1000.
    """
    function mostBuckets(): Index
        ensures result = 1000;

    """
    Whether name may name a metric: 1 to 64 bytes of a to z, 0 to 9, dot,
    hyphen and underscore.
    No contract: a walk over name; false is the answer for a bad one.
    """
    generic [N: Region]
    function isMetricName(name: Span[Nat8, N]): Bool;

    """
    Makes the table of samples and its index, if they are not there.
    No contract: the answer is the work of the database.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function prepareMetrics(db: &![Database[Writing], R]): Option[DbError];

    """
    Keeps the sample.  Right false, and nothing kept, when name is no metric
    name, value is below 0 or at below 0.
    No contract: the answer is the work of the database.
    """
    generic [R: Region, N: Region]
    function recordMetric(db: &![Database[Writing], R], name: Span[Nat8, N], at: Int64, value: Int64): Either[DbError, Bool];

    """
    The series of name: buckets buckets of step seconds from since, the
    first from since to since + step.  Samples outside are left out.  An
    empty buffer for a name that is no metric name, a step below 1 or above
    366 days, a since below 0 or no buckets; buckets above mostBuckets are cut to it.
    No contract: the answer is the work of the database.
    """
    generic [Q: Free, R: Region, N: Region]
    function series(db: &![Database[Q], R], name: Span[Nat8, N], since: Int64, step: Int64, buckets: Index,
                    fold: Fold): Either[DbError, Buffer[Int64]];

    """
    The value of the latest sample of name, or None.
    No contract: the answer is the work of the database.
    """
    generic [Q: Free, R: Region, N: Region]
    function latestMetric(db: &![Database[Q], R], name: Span[Nat8, N]): Either[DbError, Option[Int64]];

    """
    Removes the samples from before the time before; Right the number
    removed.
    No contract: the answer is the work of the database.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function pruneMetrics(db: &![Database[Writing], R], before: Int64): Either[DbError, Nat64];
end module.
